infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title pandas or polars: when each wins
  desc Same data, same logic — the choice is ecosystem-and-small-data vs pipeline-scale
  compares
    - label Keep pandas
      children
        - label Eager: materializes every line
          desc Peak memory = sum of intermediates
        - label object strings cost ~5x memory
          desc 700-900 MB vs ~150 MB Arrow per 10M
        - label Silent int to float on a gap
          desc Ids past 2^53 round; apply is a 10-100x cliff
        - label Best for ecosystem + small data
          desc scikit-learn, statsmodels, notebooks
    - label Reach for polars
      children
        - label Lazy plan: pushdown before IO
          desc Reads 2 of 40 cols, skips row groups
        - label Arrow columns, no index
          desc Contiguous typed buffers, explicit joins
        - label Strict, multi-threaded Rust
          desc No silent promotion; 5-50x on pipelines
        - label Best for scheduled pipelines
          desc Jobs over data near or above RAM
